                <pb facs="0336" n="276" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg276"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Eustis to Mr.
                            Adee</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-08-23"><hi rendition="#italic">August 23,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Minister for foreign affairs had requested me to await his return to Paris to
                    conclude arrangements about visit to Waller. He arrived on 21st, and we then
                    agreed that the legal adviser and a member of the embassy should be delegated by
                    me. To day I was notified that the necessary orders were given. To-morrow the
                    second secretary and Alexander will leave for place [of] confinement to carry
                    out your instructions by cable 22d instant.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Eustis</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
